    "opinions": [
      {
        "text": "Sup. Ct. Ohio. Certiorari denied. The Chief Justice, Mr. Justice Douglas, Mr. Justice Stewart, and Mr. Justice Fortas concur in the denial of certiorari, pointing out that the issues under Witherspoon v. Illinois, 391 U. S. 510, can be decided only upon consideration of a transcript of the voir dire of the jury, which is not now in the record but which can presumably be made available in state or federal collateral proceedings.",
